  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 108 PM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nUpper level ridge does move over the Great Basin to Four Corners\nFriday into Saturday. Synoptic ensembles are in pretty good\nagreement with this idea. The problem is that as the ridge moves\nto the west it also becomes stronger. What this means is that\nupper level heights do not drop much as the ridge moves away due\nto it strengthening at the same time. The end result means that\nhigh temperatures do not decrease much over the weekend. We will\nlikely be re-issuing heat advisories into the weekend for a lot \nof the same areas.\n\nBy early next week Monday into Tuesday the ridge does become \nweaker with lower heights meaning less subsidence. By next Tuesday\ninto Wednesday the monsoon moisture plume is more pronounced over\nSE AZ and E AZ with some moisture filtering into NM. There is not\nmuch to bank on with this scenario but the forecast does trend \ntowards slightly lower high temperatures and higher thunderstorm \nchances. There is very little confidence but New Mexico really \nneeds the precipitation.",
